{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00471",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 4.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Okay, so hello doctor, sorry, am I early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.81,
      "end_seconds": 8.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "So, you're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.61,
      "end_seconds": 17.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Right, doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.45,
      "end_seconds": 23.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.48,
      "end_seconds": 40.06,
      "duration_seconds": 15.58,
      "text": "Well, I've been having tightness in my chest when I walk. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.66,
      "end_seconds": 46.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.36,
      "end_seconds": 60.4,
      "duration_seconds": 13.04,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, you know, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.49,
      "end_seconds": 66.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.46,
      "end_seconds": 70.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.03,
      "end_seconds": 76.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 76.75,
      "end_seconds": 82.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Oh, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.12,
      "end_seconds": 85.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.99,
      "end_seconds": 90.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.38,
      "end_seconds": 97.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Right, um, there's a heavy feeling in the left arm as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.16,
      "end_seconds": 99.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "And fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.8,
      "end_seconds": 104.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Well, no, I haven't had any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 105.04,
      "end_seconds": 110.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Yeah, actually, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.62,
      "end_seconds": 116.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.57,
      "end_seconds": 124.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any pain at rest, fainting or swelling in the ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.13,
      "end_seconds": 140.6,
      "duration_seconds": 14.47,
      "text": "No, you know, no pain at rest, no fainting, no swelling in the ankles. I did have breathlessness on exertion at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.93,
      "end_seconds": 142.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Right. And cough, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.75,
      "end_seconds": 146.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.31,
      "end_seconds": 150.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.2,
      "end_seconds": 153.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Nothing there, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.75,
      "end_seconds": 161.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.37,
      "end_seconds": 186.69,
      "duration_seconds": 24.32,
      "text": "Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I did try to ignore it for a while. I took the morning off to come in today. It's telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. Clopidogrel. I take it 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.05,
      "end_seconds": 188.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.26,
      "end_seconds": 192.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Oh, I'm on rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 193.4,
      "end_seconds": 201.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the rosuvastatin was 5 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.3,
      "end_seconds": 205.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.15,
      "end_seconds": 216.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "I mean, no, I left it at home. I used to take amlodipine, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.28,
      "end_seconds": 221.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "So, do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.87,
      "end_seconds": 229.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.97,
      "end_seconds": 230.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.05,
      "end_seconds": 237.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.96,
      "end_seconds": 239.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.88,
      "end_seconds": 242.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.56,
      "end_seconds": 244.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.36,
      "end_seconds": 251.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had high cholesterol, yes. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.63,
      "end_seconds": 259.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Okay. Right, so that's your known heart disease. We'll keep that in mind today. Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.51,
      "end_seconds": 264.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Yeah, um, no, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.13,
      "end_seconds": 268.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.66,
      "end_seconds": 272.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "So, uh, of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.46,
      "end_seconds": 283.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.67,
      "end_seconds": 287.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Well, my grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.86,
      "end_seconds": 290.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.8,
      "end_seconds": 295.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Just cataract surgery on my right eye, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.64,
      "end_seconds": 301.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.71,
      "end_seconds": 306.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.27,
      "end_seconds": 317.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.39,
      "end_seconds": 320.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.98,
      "end_seconds": 339.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Lungs are clear and there's no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.16,
      "end_seconds": 360.47,
      "duration_seconds": 18.31,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Putting it all together, it fits best with angina-type chest pain. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out a musculoskeletal cause yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.07,
      "end_seconds": 371.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had tightness in your chest when you walk, and no fainting or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.21,
      "end_seconds": 374.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Well, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.44,
      "end_seconds": 380.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.37,
      "end_seconds": 394.35,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "So, um, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.96,
      "end_seconds": 403.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ECG for chest tightness. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 404.26,
      "end_seconds": 408.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "We have a slot Monday at 10 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.17,
      "end_seconds": 412.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Let's get a lipid profile, for cardiovascular risk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.49,
      "end_seconds": 415.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.46,
      "end_seconds": 441.49,
      "duration_seconds": 25.03,
      "text": "We should do an echocardiogram for chest tightness. I'd like you to take GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. That should help with chest tightness. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.47,
      "end_seconds": 450.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.58,
      "end_seconds": 453.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Okay, you know, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.27,
      "end_seconds": 462.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "If the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 463.63,
      "end_seconds": 464.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.72,
      "end_seconds": 469.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 469.74,
      "end_seconds": 470.44,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 471.6,
      "end_seconds": 474.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 475.3,
      "end_seconds": 478.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Um, I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}